{1 = 1-8}
9=1.	Lady, you who wander among sweet-voiced cows and gentle-voiced calves in the cattle-pen; young woman, no sooner will you arrive there, @wDN{Inana}, than the churn should sound! May the churn of your spouse sound, @wDN{Inana}, may the churn of @wDN{Dumuzid} sound! May the churn sound, may the churn of @wDN{Dumuzid} sound! 

{9 = 9-16}
41=9.	The rocking of the churn will sing for you, 
45=10.	@wDN{Inana}, thus making you joyous. 
49=11.	The holy churn will sound …… for you, 
53=12.	thus making you joyous, @wDN{Ninegala}. The good shepherd, 
57=13.	the man of sweet songs, 
61=14.	will loudly (?) sing songs for you; 
65=15.	lady, with the sweetest songs, @wDN{Inana}, 
69=16.	may he make your heart joyous! 

{17 = 17-22}
73=17.	Lady, when you enter the cattle-pen, @wDN{Inana}, 
77=18.	the cattle-pen indeed will rejoice over you. 
81=19.	Mistress, when you enter the sheepfold, @wDN{Inana}, 
85=20.	the sheepfold indeed will rejoice over you. 
89=21.	When you enter the feeding-pen, 
93=22.	healthy ewes will spread out their wool for you. 

{24 = 23-29}
101=23.	May your spouse, @wDN{Ama-ušumgal-ana}, 
105=24.	…… on (?) your holy breast. 
109=25.	May the holy sheepfold produce plentiful supplies of butter (?) for you. 
113=26.	It will make butter plentiful (?), it will make milk plentiful (?), 
117=27.	thus making you joyous, @wDN{Inana}. 
121=28.	May the holy sheepfold make the butter extensive (?) for you, 
29.	thus making you joyous, @wDN{Ninegala}. 

{30 = 30-35}
125=30.	For the king you have chosen with your heart, for @wDN{Dumuzid}, the son of @wDN{Enlil}, may the cattle-pen produce (?) butter and milk, may the sheepfold produce (?) abundance! May the days of the true shepherd be numerous! The true shepherd, @wDN{Dumuzid} …… days of prosperity! 

{36 = 36}
151=36.	A @fsux{balbale} of @wDN{Inana}. 
